  <text x="758" y="258" fill="#dfe3ed" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="9.5">not correct by construction. Post-fix, in flight is</text>
  <text x="758" y="271" fill="#00ff80" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700">zero — the property that actually matters.</text>

  <line x1="755" y1="282" x2="1065" y2="282" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-opacity="0.12"/>
  <text x="758" y="299" fill="#9ba3b8" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="9" font-weight="700">STATIC INSTRUCTION COST</text>
  <text x="758" y="315" fill="#ffffff" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="10">Interpreter: 5,629 → 5,848 static instructions,</text>
  <text x="758" y="329" fill="#ffb35c" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="10" font-weight="700">+3.89 %</text>
  <text x="806" y="329" fill="#dfe3ed" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="9.5">· -DV2_REGISTER: no barriers at all</text>
  <text x="758" y="344" fill="#00ff80" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700">Both builds: byte-identical at 4,457 instructions</text>
  <text x="758" y="357" fill="#dfe3ed" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="9.5">the fix costs the register tier nothing.</text>

  <!-- Consequence cascade -->
  <text x="25" y="386" fill="#9ba3b8" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="0.8">THE CONSEQUENCE CHAIN</text>
