+  <title id="title">An Execution-Only Barrier Is Not a Memory Barrier</title>
+  <desc id="desc">Broken and fixed two-wave timelines show how an unfenced LDS write can pass an execution-only barrier, corrupt a reduction, and desynchronize pseudorandom draws. An ISA audit, instruction cost, and paired performance bars quantify the fix.</desc>
